  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Staff can update a delay notice and speak with readers whose pickup is affected.\", \"decision\": \"How should a reader hear about a temporary delay?\", \"goal\": \"Keep books moving and make the afternoon service easier to use without excluding readers who arrive without an appointment.\", \"problem\": \"A small library becomes crowded during afternoon pickups and returns. It has a request sheet, adjustable pickup windows, a few trained helpers, labeled shelves, and enough room to separate several activities. Staff want a practical plan that preserves walk-in access. Each decision below concerns a different part of the service; none requires exclusive use of all helpers or space.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nA helper keeps the delay notice current while staff speak with affected readers at the same time. Shared and individual updates proceed without waiting for one another.\nStaff update the delay notice first and then speak with affected readers who want an individual update. A common message reaches everyone before personal follow-up.\nStaff speak with affected readers first and then update the delay notice with the shared explanation. The notice reflects the questions raised in those conversations."
    }
